  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14466340",
      "title": "Using Types with the HttpClient",
      "lectureOrder": 583,
      "videoOrder": 536,
      "sourceHash": "7ce9486a8c81bea9606ad2f42dc5f66d50d0cc64c0a5649ef9578f0c19c538cd",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.25,
          "end": 4.8,
          "en": "-: The next step now of course is to output our posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.8,
          "end": 8.7,
          "en": "Before we do that, however, let me bring your attention",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.7,
          "end": 10.95,
          "en": "to a tiny problem we have here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.95,
          "end": 14.7,
          "en": "or to a spot where we can improve our code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.7,
          "end": 17.7,
          "en": "If we hover over posts here in your ID,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.7,
          "end": 19.71,
          "en": "you probably see the type of posts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.71,
          "end": 21.783,
          "en": "and you see that this is of type any.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.92,
          "end": 25.08,
          "en": "That of course means the TypeScript is not able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.08,
          "end": 29.37,
          "en": "to detect how our posts look like, the format of our post.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.37,
          "end": 32.43,
          "en": "Cause here posts array all sorts of type any,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.43,
          "end": 34.14,
          "en": "because the only thing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.14,
          "end": 37.38,
          "en": "TypeScript sees is that we add the ID key here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.38,
          "end": 38.28,
          "en": "But other than that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.28,
          "end": 41.04,
          "en": "the object we push is totally unknown to it because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.04,
          "end": 43.59,
          "en": "it doesn't know the format of our response data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.59,
          "end": 45.51,
          "en": "There it only knows that it's an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.51,
          "end": 47.493,
          "en": "but not how this object looks like.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.23,
          "end": 51.72,
          "en": "We can tell TypeScript how it looks like.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.72,
          "end": 56.19,
          "en": "One way of doing it would be to assign a type here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.19,
          "end": 58.17,
          "en": "on the argument we're getting in Map.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.17,
          "end": 61.44,
          "en": "So we could say, yeah, we know that this actually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.44,
          "end": 64.39,
          "en": "will be an object where we have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.34,
          "end": 68.01,
          "en": "a randomly generated string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.01,
          "end": 71.4,
          "en": "and now this syntax can look really weird in TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.4,
          "end": 72.36,
          "en": "but in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 72.36,
          "end": 76.47,
          "en": "you use a placeholder property name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.47,
          "end": 78.69,
          "en": "for that by using square brackets here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 78.69,
          "end": 82.78,
          "en": "And then you add key colon string in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.73,
          "end": 87.57,
          "en": "which simply means this is any string key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.57,
          "end": 89.13,
          "en": "we have here on that object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 89.13,
          "end": 90.87,
          "en": "We don't know the exact property name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 90.87,
          "end": 93.78,
          "en": "because it's randomly generated or not randomly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 93.78,
          "end": 95.28,
          "en": "but it's generated by Firebase.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 95.28,
          "end": 97.11,
          "en": "And we do have many different properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 97.11,
          "end": 98.85,
          "en": "but we know it will be a property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 98.85,
          "end": 100.89,
          "en": "that can be interpreted as a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 100.89,
          "end": 103.77000000000001,
          "en": "And now the value held by that property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 103.77000000000001,
          "end": 106.11,
          "en": "is our actual post data, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 106.11,
          "end": 109.08,
          "en": "It's the same format we have here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 109.08,
          "end": 111.75,
          "en": "Now, therefore, to simplify it as a bid for us,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 111.75,
          "end": 114.662,
          "en": "we can of course add a new model.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 114.662,
          "end": 119.12899999999999,
          "en": "Let's say a post model here where I export that interface",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 119.12899999999999,
          "end": 122.186,
          "en": "and I'll name this post and this will just have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 122.186,
          "end": 125.13,
          "en": "that format here, title and content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 125.13,
          "end": 128.13,
          "en": "and actually will optionally all to have an ideal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 128.13,
          "end": 130.17,
          "en": "Let's add a quest mark here to make clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 130.17,
          "end": 132.12,
          "en": "that this is a string but it's optional",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 132.99,
          "end": 135.42,
          "en": "and now we can use that here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 135.42,
          "end": 139.26,
          "en": "So there we use post, we just need to import that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 139.26,
          "end": 140.5,
          "en": "So let's import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 141.72,
          "end": 143.26,
          "en": "post from",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 144.63,
          "end": 147,
          "en": "our post model file here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 147,
          "end": 147.97,
          "en": "So from",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 149.22,
          "end": 150.19,
          "en": "dot slash",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 151.07999999999998,
          "end": 152.463,
          "en": "post dot model.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 154.35,
          "end": 158.73,
          "en": "And now we know here we have that randomly generated ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 158.73,
          "end": 162.15,
          "en": "but that will then hold a post as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 162.15,
          "end": 164.57999999999998,
          "en": "That's that nested element I showed you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 164.57999999999998,
          "end": 166.89,
          "en": "in the developer tools earlier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 166.89,
          "end": 169.664,
          "en": "With that now TypeScript suddenly knows",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 169.664,
          "end": 172.2,
          "en": "what's inside of response data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 172.2,
          "end": 175.44,
          "en": "And now we can also set the type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 175.44,
          "end": 177.24,
          "en": "here on our post array and say, yeah,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 177.24,
          "end": 179.89,
          "en": "that will be a post array which you set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 179.89,
          "end": 182.087,
          "en": "by using this type assignment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 182.087,
          "end": 185.94,
          "en": "the name of the type, and then square brackets to indicate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 185.94,
          "end": 187.94,
          "en": "that it will be an array of these types.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 188.88,
          "end": 190.26,
          "en": "This now is improved code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 190.26,
          "end": 192.9,
          "en": "because now we can clearly understand what's inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 192.9,
          "end": 196.07999999999998,
          "en": "of posts array and we get better auto-completion.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 196.07999999999998,
          "end": 198.12,
          "en": "For example, if I try to access the first element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 198.12,
          "end": 201,
          "en": "you see I can now access ID content and title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 201,
          "end": 203.138,
          "en": "because I now know that it has this format",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 203.138,
          "end": 206.03,
          "en": "and that therefore is a recommended practice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 206.03,
          "end": 209.10399999999998,
          "en": "However, with the angler HDP Client,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 209.10399999999998,
          "end": 212.22,
          "en": "there is a more elegant way of assigning the type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 212.22,
          "end": 215.67000000000002,
          "en": "You don't need to do this here on the argument in Map or",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 215.67000000000002,
          "end": 220.23,
          "en": "in Subscribe or whatever you are using to access your data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 220.23,
          "end": 224.19,
          "en": "Instead, the get method is a so-called generic method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 224.19,
          "end": 226.53,
          "en": "This means you can add angled brackets here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 226.53,
          "end": 230.275,
          "en": "and between the angled brackets you store the type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 230.275,
          "end": 233.34,
          "en": "which this response will actually return",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 233.34,
          "end": 235.65,
          "en": "as a body once it's done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 235.65,
          "end": 238.503,
          "en": "So it's the response body type, which you store here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 238.503,
          "end": 241.32,
          "en": "and that will then automatically be handled",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 241.32,
          "end": 243.45,
          "en": "by the angler HDP Client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 243.45,
          "end": 246.24,
          "en": "and TypeScript understands this and now knows",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 246.24,
          "end": 249.15,
          "en": "that the response data will have this type format",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 249.15,
          "end": 250.2,
          "en": "as you can tell.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 250.2,
          "end": 252.66,
          "en": "And this is also available on post requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 252.66,
          "end": 254.79,
          "en": "it's available on all requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 254.79,
          "end": 257.64,
          "en": "You can use these angled brackets to add this extra piece",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 257.64,
          "end": 261.06,
          "en": "of information, which is totally optional, but recommended",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 261.06,
          "end": 264.69,
          "en": "and helpful about the data you are getting back.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 264.69,
          "end": 267.72,
          "en": "And now here you know it'll be a JavaScript object where you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 267.72,
          "end": 272.306,
          "en": "have a name property and the value of that will be a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 272.306,
          "end": 275.52,
          "en": "Because if you remember when you send a post",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 275.52,
          "end": 278.553,
          "en": "this is a new post, really new,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 279.45,
          "end": 280.38,
          "en": "the data you get back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 280.38,
          "end": 283.11,
          "en": "is exactly such an object, name, property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 283.11,
          "end": 284.76,
          "en": "and then a random string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 284.76,
          "end": 286.86,
          "en": "And now we're making this really clear here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 286.86,
          "end": 290.1,
          "en": "so that we also notice in our subscribe function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 290.1,
          "end": 293.13,
          "en": "and if we had code that depends on the types",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 293.13,
          "end": 294.81,
          "en": "we get better auto completion",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 294.81,
          "end": 297.3,
          "en": "and avoid unnecessary TypeScript errors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 297.3,
          "end": 299.73,
          "en": "So this is optional but recommended.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 299.73,
          "end": 302.28,
          "en": "You can define the response data types here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 302.28,
          "end": 305.013,
          "en": "on these generic HDP wear methods.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
